# Hug drawer actions

When adding or changing an `OsHugSheet` (hub settings children, publish access, transfer, short forms):

**Compose the settled pattern.** Copy `hub-publish-access-sheet.tsx` (or the nearest sibling hug drawer), not commerce `OsGestureSheet` + `footer`.

## Do

- Panel: `hub-manage-sheet-panel hub-manage-sheet-panel--hug` (+ `os-sheet-cap-short` for short forms)
- Body: `hub-manage-sheet-body`
- Fields + CTA inside `.hub-manage-form`
- CTA: `<OsSheetActions layout="stack" tone="frosted-primary" borderless>` wrapping `OsSheetAction` **in the body**, after the fields

```tsx
<OsHugSheet … panelClassName="… hub-manage-sheet-panel--hug …" bodyClassName="hub-manage-sheet-body">
  <div className="hub-manage-form">
    {/* fields */}
    <OsSheetActions layout="stack" tone="frosted-primary" borderless>
      <OsSheetAction …>Save</OsSheetAction>
    </OsSheetActions>
  </div>
</OsHugSheet>
```

## Do not

- Pass the primary CTA through `OsHugSheet` `footer={…}` — that uses a different pad band and reads misaligned vs publish / settings siblings
- Invent per-drawer footer padding / margin to “fix” a footer CTA
- Use full-screen `OsSlideOverScreen` / `HubManageSheetChrome` for a single short action that siblings already do as a hug drawer

Commerce buy/sell/transfer-scarce keep `OsGestureSheet` + `CommerceSheetFooter`. Hub manage hugs do not.
